@node The figure template
@section The figure template

@cindex figure template

@samp{<f} asks for the width as a fraction of @samp{\textwidth}. Pressing RET accepts
the default of 0.8. Point lands inside the braces for the image file.

@example
\begin@{figure@}[htbp]
  \centering
  \includegraphics[width=0.8\textwidth]@{@}
  \caption@{@}
  \label@{fig:@}
\end@{figure@}
@end example

@node The table template
@section The table template

@cindex table template
@cindex booktabs

@samp{<t} asks two questions and then inserts a booktabs table with the
caption above the tabular, as is usual for tables. Point lands in the
caption.

@float Table,orgebc416f
@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaa}
@headitem Prompt
@tab Meaning
@tab Default
@item Number of body rows
@tab rows below the @samp{\midrule}, header not counted
@tab 2
@item Number of columns
@tab columns, each left aligned with @samp{l}
@tab 5
@end multitable
@caption{Prompts asked by the table template.}
@end float

Pressing RET accepts the default. An answer that is not a whole number of at
least 1 is asked again. Pressing @samp{C-g} at either prompt leaves @samp{<t} in the
buffer unchanged.

Answering 3 rows and 4 columns gives

@example
\begin@{table@}[htbp]
  \centering
  \caption@{@}
  \label@{tab:@}
  \begin@{tabular@}@{llll@}
    \toprule
     & & & \\
    \midrule
     & & & \\
     & & & \\
     & & & \\
    \bottomrule
  \end@{tabular@}
\end@{table@}
@end example

Change the column letters to @samp{c}, @samp{r} or @samp{p@{3cm@}} after insertion as needed.
The defaults are set by @samp{latex-tempo-default-table-rows} and
@samp{latex-tempo-default-table-columns}.

@node Relation to the org-tempo keys
@section Relation to the org-tempo keys

@cindex org-tempo comparison

Several keys keep their Org meaning, namely @samp{<a}, @samp{<c}, @samp{<C}, @samp{<E}, @samp{<h},
@samp{<l} and @samp{<q}. The Org export blocks have no direct @LaTeX{} counterpart, so
@samp{<E} and @samp{<h} give comment environments that @LaTeX{} skips, and @samp{<l} gives a
pair of marker comments. Other keys were changed to suit @LaTeX{} writing.
@samp{<m} replaces the Org @samp{<s} source block, and @samp{<e}, @samp{<i}, @samp{<I} and @samp{<v} now
give lists, items and verbatim text.

@node Package checks
@chapter Package checks

@cindex usepackage
@cindex latex-tempo-add-usepackage

Some templates need a @LaTeX{} package. After inserting such a template,
latex-tempo searches the buffer for a matching @samp{\usepackage} or
@samp{\RequirePackage} line. Commented lines do not count.

When the line is missing and the buffer contains @samp{\begin@{document@}}, the
behavior depends on @samp{latex-tempo-add-usepackage}.

@float Table,org538e24d
@multitable {aaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Value
@tab Behavior
@item @samp{nil}
@tab show a reminder in the echo area
@item @samp{ask}
@tab ask before adding the line (the default)
@item @samp{t}
@tab add the line just above @samp{\begin@{document@}} without asking
@end multitable
@caption{Values of latex-tempo-add-usepackage.}
@end float

In a chapter file without @samp{\begin@{document@}}, such as a file read with
@samp{\input}, latex-tempo only shows a reminder.

@node Customization
@chapter Customization

@cindex customization

Run @samp{M-x customize-group RET latex-tempo RET} to see all options.

@table @asis
@item @samp{latex-tempo-templates}
The template table. See @ref{Adding your own templates}.
@item @samp{latex-tempo-default-language}
The default minted language, initially
@samp{"python"}.
@item @samp{latex-tempo-languages}
The languages offered for completion by @samp{<m}.
@item @samp{latex-tempo-default-table-rows}
The default number of body rows for
@samp{<t}, initially 2.
@item @samp{latex-tempo-default-table-columns}
The default number of columns for
@samp{<t}, initially 5.
@item @samp{latex-tempo-default-figure-width}
The default fraction of @samp{\textwidth}
for @samp{<f}, initially @samp{"0.8"}.
@item @samp{latex-tempo-add-usepackage}
See @ref{Package checks}.
@item @samp{latex-tempo-high-priority}
When non-nil, the default, TAB looks for a
template key before other minor modes such as yasnippet and
@samp{outline-minor-mode}. See @ref{Troubleshooting}.
@end table

