* Adding your own templates::
@end menu

@node Adding your own templates
@section Adding your own templates

@cindex new templates

Each entry in @samp{latex-tempo-templates} is a key string followed by a property
list. Four kinds of entries are supported.

@float Table,orgd39b449
@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Property
@tab Meaning
@item @samp{:env}
@tab environment name wrapped in @samp{\begin} and @samp{\end}
@item @samp{:open} @samp{:close}
@tab literal opening and closing lines
@item @samp{:template}
@tab list of lines, with @samp{@@@@} for point and @samp{<<arg>>} for the argument, or a function of the argument that returns such a list
@item @samp{:inline}
@tab opening string of a one-line command, ended by @samp{:close}
@item @samp{:arg}
@tab @samp{language}, @samp{width}, @samp{table-size} or @samp{file} to prompt for an argument
@item @samp{:first-line}
@tab extra line just after an @samp{:env} opening line
@item @samp{:package}
@tab @LaTeX{} package that the template needs
@item @samp{:desc}
@tab description shown in the menu
@end multitable
@caption{Properties used in latex-tempo-templates.}
@end float

This example adds @samp{<eq} for an equation environment and @samp{<al} for a
two-line align environment.

@lisp
(with-eval-after-load 'latex-tempo
  (add-to-list 'latex-tempo-templates
               '("eq" :env "equation" :desc "Equation"))
  (add-to-list 'latex-tempo-templates
               '("al" :package "amsmath"
                 :template ("\\begin@{align@}"
                            "  @@@@ &=  \\\\"
                            "     &= "
                            "\\end@{align@}")
                 :desc "Align, two lines")))
@end lisp

@node Troubleshooting
@chapter Troubleshooting

@cindex troubleshooting
@cindex yasnippet

@table @asis
@item TAB does not expand a key
Check that @samp{latex-tempo-mode} is on, which is
shown by @samp{<s} in the mode line. Check that only spaces come before the key
on the line.
@item Another package takes TAB first
Minor modes such as yasnippet and
@samp{outline-minor-mode} also bind TAB, and a minor mode loaded later normally
wins. latex-tempo avoids this by placing its keymap in
@samp{emulation-mode-map-alists}, which Emacs consults before ordinary minor
mode keymaps. TAB first checks for a template key. When there is none,
TAB runs whatever the other package bound, so yasnippet expansion and
outline cycling keep working. Set @samp{latex-tempo-high-priority} to nil to
turn this off.
@item minted fails to compile
minted needs the @samp{-shell-escape} option for
the @LaTeX{} engine.
@end table

@node Running the tests
@chapter Running the tests

@cindex tests
@cindex ERT

The repository includes an ERT test suite and a Makefile.

@float Table,org6f718c8
@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Target
@tab Action
@item @samp{make}
@tab byte-compile and run the tests
@item @samp{make test}
@tab run the ERT tests
@item @samp{make checkdoc}
@tab check documentation strings
@item @samp{make lint}
@tab run package-lint, fetched from GitHub on first use
@item @samp{make check}
@tab compile, test, checkdoc and lint
@item @samp{make doc}
@tab build the Texinfo and Info versions of this manual
@item @samp{make pdf}
@tab build a PDF version of this manual
@item @samp{make clean}
@tab remove generated files
@end multitable
@caption{Makefile targets.}
@end float

Set @samp{EMACS} to test with another Emacs, for example
@samp{make test EMACS=/Applications/Emacs.app/Contents/MacOS/Emacs}.

